ARGUMENTS: # Calendar AutoAuth MCP Server

A Model Context Protocol (MCP) server for Google Calendar integration in Cluade Desktop with auto authentication support.

## Installation & Authentication

### Installing via Smithery
```bash
npx -y @smithery/cli install @gongrzhe/server-calendar-autoauth-mcp --client claude
```

1. Create a Google Cloud Project and obtain credentials:
   a. Create a Google Cloud Project
   b. Create OAuth 2.0 Credentials (Desktop app or Web application)
   c. Download the JSON file and rename to gcp-oauth.keys.json

2. Run Authentication:
   a. Global Authentication (Recommended):
   ```bash
   mkdir -p ~/.calendar-mcp
   mv gcp-oauth.keys.json ~/.calendar-mcp/
   npx @gongrzhe/server-calendar-autoauth-mcp auth
   ```
   b. Local Authentication:
   ```bash
   npx @gongrzhe/server-calendar-autoauth-mcp auth
   ```

3. Configure in Claude Desktop:
```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "calendar": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["@gongrzhe/server-calendar-autoauth-mcp"]
    }
  }
}
```

### Docker Support
Authentication and usage via Docker with volume mounts.

